### Authentication API Tests

### 1. User Signup (Always creates ROLE_USER)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "username": "",
  "email": "",
  "password": ""
}

### 2. User Login
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
 "email": "",
  "password": ""
}

### 3. Create Admin User (requires ROLE_ADMIN authentication)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/create-admin
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer REPLACE_WITH_ADMIN_JWT_TOKEN

{
  "username": "admin",
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "AdminPass123!"
}

### 4. Admin Login
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "AdminPass123!"
}

### 5. Refresh Token (replace with actual refresh token from login)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": ""
}

### 6. Logout (requires JWT authentication only)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN
### 7. Logout from all devices (requires JWT authentication)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/logout-all
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer REPLACE_WITH_ACTUAL_JWT_TOKEN

{}

